# Aloo paratha

Filling: 3 boiled potatoes mashed, 1 small onion very finely chopped, green chilli, fresh coriander, ½ tsp anardana, ½ tsp garam masala, salt. The filling must be dry or the paratha tears.

Dough: atta, water, pinch of salt; rest 20 minutes.

Roll a small circle, put a ball of filling, close it like a pouch, flatten, roll gently. Tawa on medium; flip once, then ghee on both sides and press the edges with a spatula until crisp spots appear.

Serve with yoghurt and mango pickle.
